{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044686-potency-duration-and-multiple-practices","id":1044686,"title":"Potency/Duration and multiple Practices","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-06T13:10:40-08:00","id":1044686,"title":"Potency/Duration and multiple Practices","content":"1) Can you raise both potency and duration of a spell? Does the spell need to be fixed on the primary factor you want to raise when you opt to take penalties to raise it (can you move both potency and duration into advanced factors for a single spell?)<br /> <br /> E.g., could I spend three reaches to move potency and duration to advanced (one potency to switch so I can raise it.)<br /> <br /> 2) Can you cast spells using multiple practices within the same arcana? This mostly applies to attempting to cast a Shielded or Veiled Perfecting spell. Or would you have to cast two separate spells? I know you can cast combined spells with similar or different practices, but I was unsure about double dipping for two practices within same arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T13:50:46-08:00","id":1044705,"title":"","content":"1) Yes, and to get Advanced Potency and Advanced Duration on a spell would require only 2 Reach. Not sure why you'd switch it unless you also want the free factor bump to Primary from Arcana rating.<br /> <br /> 2) That would be a combined spell. Typically a higher level Practice can incorporate elements that seem similar to a lower level Practice though for instance Empty Presence is an invisibility spell (Typically Veiling), but does a whole lot of other shit too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T14:18:07-08:00","id":1044721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044686-potency-duration-and-multiple-practices#post1044686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Can you raise both potency and duration of a spell? Does the spell need to be fixed on the primary factor you want to raise when you opt to take penalties to raise it (can you move both potency and duration into advanced factors for a single spell?)<br /> <br /> E.g., could I spend three reaches to move potency and duration to advanced (one potency to switch so I can raise it.)<br /> <br /> 2) Can you cast spells using multiple practices within the same arcana? This mostly applies to attempting to cast a Shielded or Veiled Perfecting spell. Or would you have to cast two separate spells? I know you can cast combined spells with similar or different practices, but I was unsure about double dipping for two practices within same arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) If I'm understanding your question, yes. You can split your dice subtractions around any of the factors (taking -4 to add one to potency and to add a step to duration), and you can spend Reach to make any and all factors Advanced. Primary factor just indicates which out of potency and duration you can go up the chart for free with Highest Arcana dots -1.<br /> <br /> 2) I think you have to cast more than one spell? One spell = one Practice. I could be wrong on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-06-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:02:36-08:00","id":1044756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044686-potency-duration-and-multiple-practices?p=1044705#post1044705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Yes, and to get Advanced Potency and Advanced Duration on a spell would require only 2 Reach. Not sure why you'd switch it unless you also want the free factor bump to Primary from Arcana rating.<br /> <br /> 2) That would be a combined spell. Typically a higher level Practice can incorporate elements that seem similar to a lower level Practice though for instance Empty Presence is an invisibility spell (Typically Veiling), but does a whole lot of other shit too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Okay, so switching is only necessary in order to change which Primary factor gets the bonus! Perfect. I wasn't aware of that, so thanks to both of you for clearing that up for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) I asked myself &quot;Why would anyone NOT Veil all their spells?&quot; after I made this thread; however, the Combined Spells section on p.118 (using Mind and Forces in their example) can clear up why one might prefer one over the other: If double dipping is allowed then Mind 2 (Shielding) + Mind 3 (Perfecting) spell would utilize the lesser of two arcana requirements and levy a -2 penalty for each Practice after the first.<br /> <br /> The benefit is you share active spell slots, giving you more room to play, but you sacrifice casting pool and the extent you can push spell factors. Oh, and combined spells are limited by Gnosis, apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:05:09-08:00","id":1044758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044686-potency-duration-and-multiple-practices?p=1044721#post1044721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) If I'm understanding your question, yes. You can split your dice subtractions around any of the factors (taking -4 to add one to potency and to add a step to duration), and you can spend Reach to make any and all factors Advanced. Primary factor just indicates which out of potency and duration you can go up the chart for free with Highest Arcana dots -1.<br /> <br /> 2) I think you have to cast more than one spell? One spell = one Practice. I could be wrong on that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2) See I thought that as well, but I didn't see it explicitly written anywhere, unless I missed it, that your spells had to be limited to one Practice per arcana. Since combined spells are a thing I figured I'd ask. Turns out I was on the right track. If this is indeed the way things work, you can do a better job casting one at a time, but you can be quicker about it and give yourself some room by doing it simultaneously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T05:23:39-08:00","id":1045694,"title":"","content":"Each spell has to have one effect. That is explicitly stated in Creative Thaumaturgy. The mechanical implications of a single effect might be varied (things like Body Control have a lot of small bonuses to different things), but conceptually each spell must do one specific Thing. Shielding or Veiling your spells is a separate Thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}